; Regression: `and` and `or` are the LOGICAL operators and take bools
; (2026-10-15). Between numbers the result was typed bool and the left
; operand emitted as the branch condition: `br i64`, invalid IR that the
; in-process object writer took and `llc` refused at the seed -- found as
; `((h >> shift) and 15) as u8`, meant as the bitwise `&`.
;
; xfail: and takes bools, and its left operand is u64: the bitwise operator is &

function low_bits(h: u64) returns u8
    ((h >> 4) and 15) as u8

low_bits(255)
